    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 81
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 27,
          "type": "text",
          "title": "LogQL cheat sheet",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 13,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 82
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "Two kinds of line arrive per worker. Cloudflare emits one invocation line per request (`POST https://api.crosmos.dev/api/v1/search`) with request metadata attached as structured metadata. The application emits JSON lines with an `event` field, which is where the useful detail lives.\n\nOnly `service_name` and `deployment_environment_name` are indexed labels. Everything else (`trace_id`, `url_path`, `cloudflare_colo`, `faas_version`, ...) is structured metadata, filtered with `|` and no parser:\n\n```logql\n{service_name=\"crosmos-api-production\"} | trace_id=\"<id>\"\n{service_name=~\"crosmos-.*-production\"} | cloudflare_colo=\"SIN\"\n```\n\nApplication JSON needs `| json` first:\n\n```logql\n{service_name=\"crosmos-api-production\"} | json | event=`http.request` | status_code>=400\n{service_name=\"crosmos-ingestion-production\"} | json | event=`ingestion.source_completed` | duration_ms > 10000\n```\n\nEvent vocabulary worth knowing:\n\n- API: `http.request`, `api.request_total`, `auth.stage_completed`, `auth.failed`, `auth.refresh_reuse_detected`, `retrieval.request_started` / `retrieval.request_completed` (carries `duration_ms`, `result_count`, `top_k`), `retrieval.stage_completed`, `retrieval.signal_completed`, `retrieval.graph_seed_fanout`, `ingestion.enqueue_*`, `cron.ingestion_redrive`.\n- Ingestion: `ingestion.job_received` / `job_started` / `job_completed`, `ingestion.job_claim_skipped`, `ingestion.job_backstop_requeued`, `ingestion.source_started` / `source_completed` (carries `duration_ms`, `memory_count`, `entity_count`, `edge_count`, `source_id`, `job_id`, `trigger`), `ingestion.stage_completed` and `ingestion.orchestration_stage_completed` (carry `stage`, `status`, `duration_ms`, `input_count`, `output_count`, `transfer_bytes`, `dependency`), `ingestion.chunk_persisted`, `ingestion.batch_checkpoint`.\n\nCorrelation IDs: `trace_id` ties a log line to a Tempo trace, `request_id` ties API lines together within one request, `correlation_id` plus `job_id` / `source_id` follow an ingestion job across invocations, including across the queue hop where there is no single parent trace.\n\nPaste a trace ID into the Trace ID variable to see just that trace's lines at the bottom, then open the same ID in the Crosmos retrieval or ingestion trace dashboard for the waterfall."
          }
        }
      ]
